Revision history for Log-Munger

0.1.0   ????-??-??/??:??
        - openvpn: gate on ovpn-<instance> (Debian openvpn@.service)
        - sendmail: gate on sm-acceptingconnections
        - fail2ban: gate on fail2ban-server and accept its logger prefix,
          captured as f2b_logger
        - dovecot: match passdb failures from auth-worker, the 2.3 worker
          conn chain, and the newer auth(user,rip)<...> prefix
        - dovecot: add "Login aborted ... (code)" and prose-reason
          disconnects (submission-login)
        - dovecot: Aborted login no longer requires user=
        - dovecot: optional level on login lines (log_path output)
        - dovecot: split a trailing TLS error out of dovecot_kv as
          dovecot_tls_state / dovecot_tls_error
        - dovecot: auth failure lines now capture dovecot_service
        - exim: accept log_selector +pid prefix and I=, Ci=, X=, CV=, SNI=
          after the peer
        - exim: reject accepts unbracketed F=/recipient, "rejected after
          DATA" and a leading message id
        - exim: connect ACL "dropped by" form, captured as exim_acl_action
        - exim: add no MAIL, SMTP protocol error, synchronization error,
          sender/recipient verify fail, reverse/forward DNS lookup failures,
          local_scan() rejects and SA-Exim SA: Action lines
        - asterisk: prefix accepts older forms (no line/function, no "in",
          no colon after thread id), dialplan Log() lines and the
          full/messages file timestamp
        - asterisk: security events take the last LocalAddress and
          RemoteAddress, so a forged one injected via a client-supplied
          field no longer sets asterisk_src_ip
        - asterisk: Request failed accepts no method and quotes in From
        - asterisk: add chan_sip registration failure, extension not found,
          IAX2 and AMI auth failures, hacking attempt, and FreePBX unknown
          SIP connection
        - sshd: usernames may contain spaces and the last " from <ip>" wins,
          so a forged address in the username no longer sets ssh_src_ip;
          same for the Bad protocol identifier
        - sshd: port optional on Failed, Connection closed and disconnects
        - sshd: Received disconnect captures ssh_disconnect_code and
          ssh_disconnect_reason, and takes an error: prefix
        - sshd: User ... not allowed takes a hostname (UseDNS), PAM errors
          take " via <ip>"
        - sshd: old "Disconnecting: Too many authentication failures" form,
          fatal: prefix on Unable to negotiate
        - sshd: add Disconnecting <state> user, ssh_dispatch_run_fatal,
          ROOT LOGIN REFUSED, tcp_wrappers refused connect and a catch-all
          for error:/fatal: lines with no function name
        - postfix: smtpd reject matches milter-reject and a syslog-truncated
          line with no "; from=... to=..." tail
        - postfix: improper command pipelining no longer needs trailing data
        - postfix: add too many errors after, anvil rate/concurrency limit
          warnings and hostname does not resolve warnings, each capturing
          the client address
        - mysql: accept the MySQL 5.5 YYMMDD date, MariaDB space-padded hour
          and a prefix with no thread id
        - openvpn: client-instance restarting (SIGUSR1) matched, captured as
          openvpn_client_instance; the signal name may contain digits
        - openvpn: add tls-auth/tls-crypt "TLS Error: ... from [AF]ip:port"
          and "TLS Auth Error" username/password failures
        - vsftpd: [pid N] optional (syslog_enable=YES), ::ffff: mapped
          client addresses unwrapped, FAIL LOGIN refusal reason captured as
          vsftpd_reason
        - pam: match the pre-0.99 "(pam_unix) " and "pam_unix: " prefixes and
          a bare "authentication failure; logname=..." line

0.0.1   2026-08-23/17:00
        - init
